WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.670
Team Quadrifoglio...

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.330
Congratulations

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.920
Congratulations on getting 
through the first fight!

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.130
Th-Thank you!

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.670
Make sure you clean that up, Manager.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.140
O-Of course.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.960
With an opponent of that level, 
it's natural that I won.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.780
Sheesh! Ya show-off!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.350
After all, if I'd been able to fight...

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.810
It's settled! Next time, I'm going first!

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.110
I'm not lettin' you be the only 
one who gets to play Mr. Cool!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.230
Hmph.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.010
Huh?

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.760
Kamui!

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.820
Ulp!

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.710
Congratulations on winning the first fight!

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.960
Argggh!

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.820
Uwaaa!

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.290
Cut it out! Get offa me! Go away!

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.050
I can't help being happy!

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.590
Well, I'm not!

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.150
I didn't get to fight, for one thing...

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.420
And for another, you're 
getting way too close!

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.140
Oh, you're so bashful!

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.630
But I think you'd be better 
off not fighting, Kamui.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.310
What's that supposed to mean?

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.110
Well, after all, you'd have no 
chance against my big brother!

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.670
But I'd better get going!

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.070
Mm?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.370
Huh?

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:00.660
Eh?

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.750
Gouki...

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.680
Vanguard Championship
Third Kanto Region Tournament

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.730
And now, the final fight of this first round!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.080
Our fighters are...

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.210
a team made up of experts in flower 
arrangement, tea ceremony, and calligraphy...

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:48.640
Victory

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.820
Team Nadeshiko!

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.220
And representing Card Shop 
Handsome, Team Handsome!

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.510
These are our two teams!

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.710
All right, for the first match, 
the two teams' fighters are...

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.990
From Team Nadeshiko, an expert 
in tea ceremony, Hiromi Sakyuin!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.850
And facing her, from Team 
Handsome, Gouki Daimonji!

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.760
Gouki's going first?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.270
Shouldn't their strongest fighter go last?

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:14.890
If he wants to get the team pumped by 
winning the first match, then this way works.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.030
As you said, though, Aichi, putting 
the strongest fighter last,

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:23.110
so that the other two can be more relaxed 
when they fight, is another way.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:28.550
Sometimes the whole fight rides on 
deciding the order of the players.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.060
There's actually more than meets the 
eye when it comes to a team fight.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.870
That stuff has nothin' to do with me!

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.520
Since I ain't gonna lose to anyone!

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.030
Kamui, you're so cool!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.990
White-Hot Tournament!

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.690
Knock it off!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.830
The winner, Gouki Daimonji!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.830
Wow...

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.350
See?! My big brother's strong, right?!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.830
I know that...

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.900
It kind of feels like he's gotten 
stronger since last time.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.220
Of course. Everyone improves.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.300
That's why fights are exciting.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:07.470
I wanted to become strong 
enough to beat Gouki...

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.010
But it seems like I've got a long road ahead.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.030
Ka-boom!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.190
Complete defeat!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.400
That's the game!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.740
Team Handsome wins the second match, too!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.450
As you might expect, last year's champions 
have smoothly advanced to the second fight!

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.010
Team Handsome vs. Team Nadeshiko

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:32.080
If we fight them, it'll be in the 
final game of the tournament.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.170
Watch out, Gouki! I'm gonna 
destroy Team Handsome!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.680
Kamui, you're so cool!

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.340
Stop it!

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.450
Okay, with the first fight done, 
let's move right on to fight two!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.630
And who do we have for this 
first match of our second fight?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.160
Team Martial Arts versus Team Q4!

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.100
Something to look forward to, isn't it?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:50.820
Yeah.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.770
I'm excited, ka-boom!

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:54.690
Kamui...

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:59.710
Both teams showed fantastic 
strength in their first fights.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.610
I'm first, Kai's up second...

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.000
and you're last, Brother, okay?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.540
Yeah. Good luck!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.530
Good luck, Kamui!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.240
If only that were Miss Emi cheering me on...

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:24.320
Never mind! Right now, I've gotta 
focus on my Vanguard fight!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:29.190
If I win, win, and win again, there's no 
doubt Miss Emi will come running to root for me!

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:30.720
Here I go!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.240
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.780
I'm gonna show you my power!

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.080
I swear by the sign of my 
training hall that I'll win!

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.340
I ride Bloody Hercules!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.010
And then I call Lady Bomb!

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.990
Lady Bomb's counterblast!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.590
Your Queen of Hearts can't stand next turn!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:06.120
Bloody Hercules is boosted by Bahr...

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.330
and attacks Tough Boy!

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.730
Drive trigger check!

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.400
Damage trigger check!

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.100
Stand trigger!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.980
Queen of Hearts stands!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.500
Too bad!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.080
No matter how many times they go 
down, Nova Grapplers always rise up,

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.290
so against them, that 
skill means diddly-squat!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.250
That was wonderful, Kamui!

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.490
If you win, I'll pat you on the head!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:36.390
Ack!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.500
We each have 5 damage...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.540
He has two cards in his hand...

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.310
I'll win it with this!

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:51.430
I release that raging, evil soul!

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.270
I ride Genocide Jack!

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.430
Three Genocide Jacks?!

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.550
Brute force, eh?

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.070
Genocide Jack, triple rev into high gear!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.820
Now all three of them can attack!

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.090
Count 1!

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:15.080
Genocide Jack is boosted 
by the Queen of Hearts...

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.080
and attacks Hell Spider!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.470
I defend with the Lizard Soldier, Ganlu!

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.860
Count 2!

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.830
Genocide Jack, boosted by the 
Queen of Hearts, attacks!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.870
When Genocide Jack is Vanguard 
and boosted by a Nova Grappler,

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:32.100
his power is +5000!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.930
I defend with Phantom Black!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.810
I intercept with Lady 
Bomb and Bloody Hercules!

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:40.890
Drive trigger check!

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:56.060
I attack with Genocide Jack, 
boosted by Lucky Girl!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.370
Finishing hold!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.000
Damage trigger check!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.010
Count 3!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.800
The winner: Kamui Katsuragi!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.070
He did it!

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:13.110
Yayyy!

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.230
Kamui!

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:16.120
I did it, Brother!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:16.550
Yep!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.310
Okay, the second matchup of the first fight!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.190
Victory...

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:45.150
The winner, Toshiki Kai of Team Q4!

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:54.120
Rats! He oughta at least 
have a tough match! Jerk!

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.150
Yesss! With two wins in a row, 
we move on to the next fight.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:58.510
Kai and Kamui really are strong!

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.240
Huh?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.000
Oh, nothing!

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.910
I may not get any more playing time,

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.030
but I'll be happy if our team wins.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.270
Huh?

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.480
Take the signs of our training halls.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.390
Uh, I couldn't...

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.770
Team Q4 beat Team Martial 
Arts two fights in a row!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.870
In their debut appearance, they've made it to 
the semifinals, but now, ready to take them on...

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.710
...in lab coats, the strong 
Team Chemistry Club!

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.770
The result of the first 
fight of the semifinals!

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.410
Team Chemistry Club
First  Flask Sato
Second  Measuring Cylinder Tanaka
Third  Beaker Suzuki

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.870
The winner is Team Q4!

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:47.460
Team Q4
First  Kamui Katsuragi
Second  Toshiki Kai
Third  Aichi Sendou

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.680
The liquid components that 
come out of tear glands are...

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.570
H20...

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.530
NaCl...

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:55.400
Alright!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.320
Wow!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.820
The finals are up next!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.140
Kamui the Great, you're awesome!

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:01.150
KA, yo!

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.910
Both of you guys were great!

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.940
This is amazing! I never believed 
we'd be able to get to the finals!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.090
Of course!

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.390
But not because of you, 
Kai. It's thanks to me!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.070
Haha...

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.940
For better or worse, they're playing 
to the best of their abilities...

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.640
The second fight of the semifinals 
is sure to be another heated battle!

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:24.410
Yakisoba Mori
Yakiudon Sanuki
Yakipasta Nabori

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.730
Team Hot Noodles is cornered!

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.920
It's the second match, with 
Team Handsome's Gouki Daimonji!

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.580
The winner, Team Handsome!

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:43.420
Just what you'd expect from 
last year's winning team!

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.640
Their overwhelming strength 
led them to victory!

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:49.050
I'm sure today's noodles will be salty!

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.090
Yeah...

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:53.300
And now we have our final two teams!

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:58.580
Which team will take away the crown 
of victory: Team Q4 or Team Handsome?!

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.910
Kamui... You've come all this way...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.680
Sorry I kept you waiting, Gouki.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.020
Good luck, Kamui!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.700
Don't ruin a dramatic moment!

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.020
I even love your angry shout!

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:28.570
The finals of the regional tournament will 
be held in the afternoon, after a break.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:29.710
I repeat...

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.790
The finals of the regional tournament 
will be held in the afternoon...

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.780
Huh?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.300
Kamui!

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:41.880
Where are you?!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.360
Don't hide on me! Come out!

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.080
Kamui!

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.600
The time to crush Team 
Handsome has finally come.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.980
Brace yourself, Gouki.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:02.530
Heh! Kamui, I really wanted to fight 
alongside you, on the same team.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:07.510
I'm grateful to you for giving me the 
opportunity to get started with this.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:13.240
I was ticked off at some kids, who acted 
big just because they were older than me...

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.640
But it didn't matter.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.120
Size and strength made all the difference.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.120
That's when I first saw you...

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.860
Kicking an adult's butt in a Vanguard fight.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.230
Drive check!

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.340
I lose!

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.670
You've gotten stronger!

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.690
Here, this is what you've wanted, right?

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:52.950
I can really have it?

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:53.380
Huh?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.520
That's one ugly kisser!

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.840
You told me that in a Vanguard fight, 
a person's size didn't really matter.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.180
I remember.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.260
I wanna fight against you, no holds barred!

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.400
That's how I'll settle my old score with you.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:22.140
Uh, I think you wanna say, "pay you back".

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:23.900
I'm going first.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.770
Gotcha.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.920
Once I am your foe, I'm gonna 
take you down with all I've got!

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.420
Oh yeah?! Not if I crush 
you like a bug first!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.810
Whaaat?!

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:37.540
You forgot to bring lunch?!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.640
I'm sorry!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:45.750
Apparently, I got it mixed up with the 
sub-manager's lunch, and brought that instead...

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.130
How could you get them mixed up?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.840
And I did my best to make it...

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:53.830
Red and white fish paste, rolled omelet, 
mashed sweet potatoes with chestnuts...

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.100
New Year's food?!

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:58.300
What do you think? Give this a shot?

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.100
N-No, I'll pass...

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.920
Um, you can have this, if you'd like.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.070
Could that voice be...?!

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.050
Miss Emi!

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.180
Emi?! What are you doing here?

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:14.110
Mom told me to bring lunch.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:16.920
Th-Thank you, Miss Emi!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.420
It looks delicious!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.780
Thanks, Emi.

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:23.430
You saved us. Thank you, Emi.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.770
Aichi, how are the fights going?

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:26.870
Perfectly!

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:28.840
Yep! The final fight is up next.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.580
That's wonderful!

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:33.850
Kai and Katsuragi must be really strong.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.780
Th-That's true.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.240
Certainly, you're right...

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.030
Your brother is strong, too!

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.040
He won the first fight, no problem!

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.770
Also, if you'd call me Kamui,

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:47.170
I-I-I'd be really happy...

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.320
Here.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.760
She wasn't listening...

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.820
Th-Thank you!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.720
A-After eating this sandwich made with love,

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.850
I'll win the final fight for sure!

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.070
Aaaah!

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:01.050
Kamui, I found you!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:05.000
Here's your beloved wife's lunch! Eat up!!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.400
Maybe I'll give Aichi some advice...

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.120
Gulp!

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.000
My love-packed sandwich!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:23.640
Give it back!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.860
W-What's your problem?!

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.440
After she gave <i>me</i> that 
sandwich made with love!

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.610
There's no need to be that angry!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.320
<i>I</i> made you lunch!

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.370
Lunch...

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:44.080
What the heck was that about?!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.420
Ta-daa! It's your face, Kamui!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.570
Doesn't it look yummy?!

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:51.670
Eat!

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:55.360
That little turd is pretty popular...

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.300
N-No way!!

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:58.780
Kamui!

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.790
No! No! No-no-no-no-no-no-no-no!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.460
You're so bashful!

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:06.230
W-What the...?!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.950
Spicyyyyyy!!

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:15.860
What did you put in there?

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:20.020
Wasabi, mustard, pepper sauce, and cayenne!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.970
Anyway, a lot of spicy stuff!

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:24.460
You like spicy food, don't you, Kamui?

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.370
You were gonna have me eat that stuff?!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.080
Sorry!

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:30.160
Kamui!

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.360
L-Let me go!

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.580
Never!

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:34.430
Um, Miss Emi...

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.410
Th-This is...

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.770
Kamui's sweetheart!

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:41.520
That's right! We're gonna get married soon!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.120
No, we ain't! And you ain't my sweetheart!

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.590
The girl I love is...

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.420
Nagisa, right?!

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.660
Wrong!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:50.710
Nagisa!

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:51.730
No!

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:52.850
It's Nagisa!

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:56.080
Nooo! I love...

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:56.880
Mm?

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.500
Mi...ss...E...

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.650
...mi...

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:02.480
Mm?

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.270
Huh?

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:12.800
Kamui is mine!

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.920
Nyaaah!

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.420
Eh?

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.920
It's tough to be a popular man.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.250
Um, uh...

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.810
W-What are you doing?!

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.440
I'm sorry, Miss Emi! You 
shouldn't have had to see that!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.160
And moreover, that sandwich 
you made for me...

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.950
That Lose-umi ate it!

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:35.000
Uh...

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.810
This is revolting!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:37.940
That's it.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.410
I'm calling a showdown!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.380
Huh?!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.480
The final fight of the regional 
tournament will begin shortly.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:49.080
All competitors, please meet 
at the designated area.

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:50.800
This is it.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:53.250
Mm?

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:55.030
Misaki!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:56.690
Huh?

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.840
We've been waiting for you.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:06.210
Misaki, why weren't you 
here from the beginning?

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.710
I thought for sure you 
were going to be here...

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.610
So when you didn't show, I had a rough time.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:13.190
Sorry. How did it go?

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.980
I won somehow.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:18.740
And thanks to Kai and Kamui's success, 
we're heading into the finals right now.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.100
Really?

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.730
You will play in the final 
fight, won't you, Misaki?

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:26.830
You've come this far, so 
stay in it to the end.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:30.920
Okay. I'll fight.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.350
Although I'm sure you won't get the chance 
to, Brother Aichi, even in the final fight.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:37.760
Me and Kai here are gonna win 
it with two takedowns in a row.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.300
Sure thing.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.520
If the team wins, that's good enough for me.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.720
Well, shall we go, everyone?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:45.740
Yes!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:46.940
Yeahhh!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.960
At last, all that's left of this 
regional tournament is the final fight!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.390
Final
Team Handsome vs Team Q4

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:03.810
But before that, let's warm up 
with the tournament's theme song!

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:08.740
The debut song by those 
up-and-coming idols, Ultra-rare!

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:12.460
"Miracle Trigger, Tomorrow 
Will Be Ultra-rare!"

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.670
Enthusiastic curiosity

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:19.470
Be strong and decide

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.340
Running heart

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.710
Which are you watching?

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:27.500
You're serious and that's why

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.830
You'll be able to smile

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.570
It's not

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.440
- What the heck is Lose-umi doing?!
- your fault!

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:39.650
5-4, you need a chance

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:42.280
Seems like something pretty good

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.950
For your original destiny

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.500
It's Miracle Trigger Check Time!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.910
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.750
Stardust Trumpeter!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:00.880
Here.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.460
You're giving me this card?

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.510
A memento of your visit here.

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:09.120
She <i>can't</i> be the same person!

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:16.900
Thank you!

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.240
Ultraaa!!

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.220
Rekka, you were off key.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:24.250
I was not!

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.060
That boy was able to make it to the finals!

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.540
Huh? Oh, I remember him.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.630
I wonder if he's using the card I gave him.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:33.660
Yeah.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:40.240
These two teams made it to the 
regional tournament finals!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.440
Making their debut, Team Quadrafolio!

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.110
Q4, for short!

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.000
Like the four-leaf clover 
from whence their name comes,

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.290
will they be able to grasp the 
good fortune called "victory"?!

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:52.570
Against them is the sure 
bet that you all know!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:56.520
The team that won last year's regional 
championship and did great at nationals, too...

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.770
Gouki Daimonji and his Team Handsome!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:03.430
What's Nagisa doing there?

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.600
Alright!

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:07.890
Both teams have won in a sweep!

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.490
What kind of fight will they show us now?!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.370
Which one will win?!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.110
Man, that guy's kewl!

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:15.440
If you say so...

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.440
Contestants for the first 
match, step forward.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.310
I'm off, Brother Aichi!

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.710
Good luck!

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:29.350
If I knew I'd get the chance to meet Kourin,

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:33.180
I wouldn't have ceded my spot as 
shop representative to stupid Kamui!

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.880
Y'know, I never get tired of watching you.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:39.450
Miss Emi, I hope you watch my cool moves!

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.540
Please join us in cheering him on, Goddess!

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:42.840
Uh, sure.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:44.170
Do your best!

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.080
Give it your all!

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.080
I-I will!

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.880
I'll do my very best!

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:57.620
Finally, the time to beat 
Team Handsome has come!

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.840
I'm going first.

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:03.550
Gouki, there's gonna be no holding back!

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:06.080
Huh?

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:08.210
I'm your opponent.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.090
Nagisa?!

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:11.200
No way!

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:14.270
If I win, we're getting married, okay?!

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:15.270
Ulp!

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.700
Aaaaaah!

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:53.380
The final fight! It's like a dream!

00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:56.220
The inside of my mouth still burns!

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:58.000
Kamui and Kai may just win this!

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.940
What are you talking about, Aichi?!

00:23:59.940 --> 00:24:01.290
That would be too easy!

00:24:01.530 --> 00:24:03.830
Uh, but Kai and Kamui are really strong...

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:04.780
You're so naive!

00:24:04.780 --> 00:24:07.310
Listen! This is the age when 
a sandwich and lunch box

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:08.570
can fall from the sky when you're walking!

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:09.860
Uh, that was...

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:12.590
Next time: Showdown! Nova Grappler!

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:15.070
Huh? Kamui's opponent...

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:17.510
A white building, the sound 
of bells ringing out...

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.050
What kind of image is that?!
